# Batatis — Building Codes Challenge

Alberta Built World Tech Venture Pilots 2026. Repo goal: AI assistant for **alternative solution / variance applications**.

## Problem

Prescriptive codes vs innovators. Applicants must prove ≈equivalent or better performance. Many first submissions are incomplete → weeks–months of SCO back-and-forth across **430+** jurisdictions.

## Prototype target

Guide users through **Safety Codes Variance Template Part 1, Sections A–D**:

1. **Intake** — applicant + building/location facts (A–B); ask for missing/ambiguous info; separate facts vs assumptions; signal confidence.
2. **Code identification** — select/rank relevant articles; propose benchmark acceptable solution + explanation; real citations only.
3. **Section C** — once articles known, **deterministic lookup** of objective, functional statement, intent; explainer per article.
4. **Section D recommendations** — what evidence must address; flag licensed professional / engineering practice; **do not invent professional judgment**.
5. **Completeness review** — applicant or SCO; administrative gaps only.
6. **Export** — PDF matching template; portable data for local jurisdiction variants + SCO reviewer view.

Start with **NBC(AE) 2023, 2nd printing** before other codes. Division **C §2.3** = admin documentation bottleneck for alternative solutions.

## Hard stops

- Completeness ≠ technical correctness / safety certification.
- No fabricated article numbers.
- NRC code text is copyrighted (link; don’t wholesale redistribute). STANDATA is OGL-Alberta.
